Revision history for Perl extension Text-ANSI-Image

0.02 2026-11-26T06:12:56Z

    - The osc option puts a private OSC at the beginning of each row
      of a kitty image, which tells the id, the size in cells and the
      file of the image, for a program which draws the image itself,
      as ansi2pdf
    - The manual of ansipic tells the terminals that show images, and
      gives -X to less

0.01 2026-11-25T10:12:34Z

    - Text::ANSI::Image draws an image in the terminal as lines of
      text, which can be laid out and paged like any other text.  A
      method is a module Text::ANSI::Image::NAME; the first is kitty,
      the Unicode placeholders of the kitty graphics protocol (kitty,
      Ghostty, iTerm2 3.7.3 or later)
    - ansipic, the command, and App::ansipic, the command as a
      function, which Command::Run can call

